> what is the current geological era
**assistant**:
> The current geological era is the Cenozoic Era. It began around 66 million years ago following the mass extinction event that ended the Mesozoic Era and the reign of the dinosaurs. We are currently in the Holocene Epoch, which started about 11,700 years ago after the last major ice age. Some scientists also refer to the current period as the Anthropocene, recognizing the significant impact humans have on Earth's geology and ecosystems, although this is not yet an officially designated epoch.
